<title>JAPAN: Japan end-Nov coffee stocks fall 13.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan end-Nov coffee stocks fall 13.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's warehouse stocks of coffee at the end of November totalled 59,443 tonnes, down 13.1 percent from a year earlier, the Agriculture Ministry said.</p>
<p>At the end of November in 1995, stocks in Japan, the world's third-biggest coffee consumer after the United States and Germany, were 68,382 tonnes, the ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Details of the coffee stocks were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Nov 96	  Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Brazil	     10,922	  10,049	15,918</p>
<p> Colombia	   12,921	  15,093	13,454</p>
<p> Indonesia	  10,668	  10,929	11,041</p>
<p> Central America  12,787	  15,070	14,635</p>
<p> Others	     12,145	  13,692	13,334</p>
<p> Total		59,443	  64,833	68,382</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
